From: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: qca808x: disable hibernation on QCA8081

The QCA8081 comes out of reset with hibernation enabled
(QCA808X_DBG_AN_TEST bit 15): about 10s after the cable is removed it
powers itself down and only wakes up again on link pulses from a
partner. The driver already clears this bit for the duration of a cable
test, but otherwise leaves it enabled.

On AR803x PHYs the same feature also stops the clock towards the MAC,
which is why the at803x driver lets boards turn it off
("qca,disable-hibernation-mode"). Turn it off on QCA8081 in
config_init(), which also runs again after every soft reset and resume,
so the PHY and its SerDes link to the PCS stay up while the port has no
cable. This costs some idle power on an unplugged port.

QCA8084 has its own config_init() and is not affected.

Signed-off-by: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c
@@ -434,6 +434,15 @@ static int qca808x_config_init(struct ph
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/* Hibernation is enabled after reset and powers the PHY down about
+	 * 10s after the cable is removed. Keep it disabled; the cable test
+	 * clears the same bit.
+	 */
+	ret = at803x_debug_reg_mask(phydev, QCA808X_DBG_AN_TEST,
+				    QCA808X_HIBERNATION_EN, 0);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
 	/* Configure adc threshold as 100mv for the link 10M */
 	return at803x_debug_reg_mask(phydev, QCA808X_PHY_DEBUG_ADC_THRESHOLD,
 				     QCA808X_ADC_THRESHOLD_MASK,
